+## False positives
+
+Each is flagged by `appsec-review.review-signal.sink.csharp-process-shell` under appsec-review
+`rules/semgrep/review-signals.yml` (the only mounted rule that reports C# constructs) and refuted
+by a code-intelligence fact. Each lives in its own function in `src/ShellHelpers.cs`.
+
+| Id | Where | Flagged by | Refuted by |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| FP-1 | `WarmCache`: `Process.Start("/bin/sh", "-c " + "sync")` | `appsec-review.review-signal.sink.csharp-process-shell` | constant operand: no `dataflow_path` reaches the sink |
+| FP-2 | `SetLogLevel`: `Process.Start("/bin/sh", "-c logger -p " + level)` | `appsec-review.review-signal.sink.csharp-process-shell` | `guard_fact`: `level >= 0 && level <= 3` dominates the sink and constrains its operand (`range_fact` 0..3) |
+| FP-3 | `StatUpload`: `Process.Start("/usr/bin/stat", "--format=%s -- " + Path.Combine(UploadRoot, safe))` | `appsec-review.review-signal.sink.csharp-process-shell` | `path_sanitizers`: `Path.GetFileName` dominates the only operand; no shell runs and `--` ends option parsing |
+| FP-4 | `LegacyShell`: `Process.Start("/bin/sh", "-c " + arg)` | `appsec-review.review-signal.sink.csharp-process-shell` | dead code: no callers, no entry point, so no `dataflow_path` reaches it |
