+## High-complexity function
+
+`Dispatch` in `src/MaintenanceController.cs` is the verb switch of the maintenance controller and
+the function the history touches most. It holds TP-C7. Its intended cyclomatic complexity is above
+15 by the appsec-review counter (branches, loops, boolean operators and conditional expressions);
+the measured value is recorded in the guide.
+
+## Code-intelligence cases
+
+`src/Program.cs` carries the appsec-review C# graph-export fixture unchanged: interface dispatch
+(`store.Load` resolving to `FileStore.Load` and `MemoryStore.Load`), delegate dispatch
+(`Helpers.Apply`), an unresolved `dynamic` call (`sink.Flush`), a sanitized path
+(`Path.GetFileName` before `File.Delete` in `Read`), a dominating and a non-dominating guard
+(`tool.Length < 16` in `Run`), a bounded allocation (`new byte[count]`) and an unguarded narrowing
+conversion (`(int)length`), command-line and environment sources in `Main`, and the cross-function
+flow summaries of `FileStore.Load` and `Helpers.Wrap`. The fixed state of `ReadReport` adds a
+second `Path.GetFileName` sanitizer and `SetLogLevel` a dominating range guard.
+
